<%# Light/dark switch, in both navs.

    Rendered hidden: without JS it is a button that cannot do anything, and
    the page is entirely usable in the default theme. script.js unhides it,
    labels it for whichever theme is active, and persists the choice — see
    partial/head.ejs for the re-apply that keeps the meta-refresh from
    flashing the other theme. %>
<button type="button"
        class="theme-toggle"
        id="theme-toggle"
        hidden
        aria-label="Switch between the light and dark theme"
        title="Switch between the light and dark theme"></button>
